 number of  abortions liberals believe the way to  reduce the number of abortions while  they should be Lee  goal is to teach reasonable sex  education not abstinence only and make  birth control available and make sure  people know how to use it  conservatives generally want to reduce  the number of abortions but they say the  way to do it is you teach abstinence  only sex education and you don't make  birth control easily accessible because  that'll encourage people to have sex now  okay those are two divergent views the  facts though when we look at studies  show that actually the liberal  prescription for reducing abortion works  whereas the conservative one doesn't so  tell us where are the incoherent parts  of either or both okay well I with  regard to abortion I think for example  if you look at conservatives you know  often they're defending individual  liberty and the right of a person to  control their own body in a pretty  fundamentalist way right right now that  is exactly the sort of defense of  abortion that you get on the Left  however I will say this about the left  they're enthusiastic as hell about all  kinds of restrictions on all kinds of  people by the state and if they're  defending abortion on the grounds that a  person has a more or less absolute right  to control their own body hmm then I  would like to see that principle  maintained consistently throughout a  series of leftist positions because what  I feel is that the left is basically  extremely enthusiastic about state power  as a solution to any given problem  except in a case for example like  abortion where they hop off and decide  that individual rights are important you  know that's fair and we have to say  though when we make that analysis the  exact inconsistency I would argue to a  greater degree exists on the right which  is well we don't want the government  getting involved except when all of a  sudden we want to prevent two men from  getting married all of a sudden were  hey 